  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2025 grant-Foster Youth Employment&amp;Entreprenuersh</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will focus on inclusion in agri-food markets, skills development, financial access, and a supportive business environment. It aims to improve climate resilience, gender equality, and food security and nutrition, aligning with the Embassy of Ireland&#x2019;s Mission Strategy (2023-2027). Activities will include skills training, peer mentorship, partnerships, access to finance, and digital tools. The project targets young women and men in Chipata, Petauke, Nyimba (Eastern Province) and Kabwe, Mpongwe (Central Province), aiming to address barriers to youth employment in the agri-food sector. It seeks to create 4,000 employment opportunities (50% for women) and support 550 youth and women-led enterprises.</narrative>
  </description>
